      "acceptance_evidence": [
        {
          "criterion": "AC-310-01",
          "result": "passed",
          "reference": "The actor-isolated registry authenticates the current peer UID, private 0600 socket posture, and per-launch challenge digest; validates bounded leases and roots; rejects stale, duplicate, cross-task, and spoofed registrations; expires and ends sessions without persisting a secret. Process identity is PID plus start time, preventing PID reuse collisions. The macOS libproc inspector captures the live process and bounded ancestry. Correlation links unique descendants at tool-linked confidence, downgrades unique workspace/time matches to inferred, leaves ambiguous overlapping tasks unknown, ignores expired registrations, and sums only evidence assigned to the requested task."
        }
      ],
      "discovered_risks": [
        "Local ancestry snapshots are point-in-time; processes that exit before inspection may require the optional privileged event observer for stronger evidence.",
        "The registry is in-memory by design and must be exposed only behind the private authenticated IPC service implemented by the connector node.",
        "Workspace-only correlations are intentionally inferred, and overlapping workspaces intentionally produce unknown rather than choosing a task."
      ],
